# SCAN-37: A scan interrupted by process death resumes and completes.
#
# launch-task, not launch-view. The scan is driven by HomeActivity, so the
# scenario resumes the existing task from the launcher rather than opening a
# document. There is no saved instance state to restore here: the assertion is
# about what LibraryScanner persisted to ScannedPdfCache before it died, and
# about the fresh pipeline finishing the work on the next launch.
#
# The kill is host driven because instrumentation shares the app process, so a
# test cannot force-stop the app without taking itself with it. Every count in
# both phases is scoped to the huge fixture's path prefix, per the scan scope
# rule, because ScannedPdfCache legitimately holds rows outside any test scope.
describe A scan interrupted by process death resumes and completes

# Seeds the scan scope, starts the 500 file first scan, and asserts the partial
# rows written so far all point at files that exist.
phase com.gitlab.mudlej.MjPdfReader.suite.scan.Scan37ProcessDeathTest#phaseOneCommitsOneResultAndLeavesDurablePendingWork

kill-app
launch-task

# Asserts the resumed pipeline reaches all 500 rows with no duplicate paths and
# an identity on every row.
phase com.gitlab.mudlej.MjPdfReader.suite.scan.Scan37ProcessDeathTest#phaseTwoReconstructsOnlyPendingWorkAndCompletesTheScan
